| WrittenBy=Jess Oppenheimer, Madelyn Pugh and Bob Carroll, Jr.
| Aux3=September 24, 1953
| OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1953|10|26}}
| ShortSummary=Tired of Ricky and Fred's attitude towards them, the girls demand equal rights. Ricky and Fred turn the tables on them when, out to dinner, they call for separate checks. Since Ethel and Lucy have no money, they must wash dishes to pay for their meals. To get even, they call their husbands from the restaurant and fake a robbery to scare them, but Ricky and Fred soon see through the scheme and get back at them by impersonating the fake robbers, only to get mistaken for real ones by the police. Lucy and Ethel get one last jab in by playing along with Ricky's ruse before everyone makes amends.
| LineColor=8AC1FF
}}
